WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.380
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit
7: Nature and the Environment.

2
00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:11.317
Unit 7 follows Amal, Nora and Teacher Yasmin from
the coast to the forest and up a mountain trail.

3
00:00:11.397 --> 00:00:17.972
You will meet fifteen nature words, from climate
and temperature to matter, energy and planet.

4
00:00:18.052 --> 00:00:25.334
You will use the present perfect to say what they
have seen, explored and visited, ask “Have you ever…?”

5
00:00:25.414 --> 00:00:30.714
questions, and build describing phrases
such as “a metal rock on the beach”.

6
00:00:30.794 --> 00:00:36.732
The unit closes with clear instructions and
a short poem about caring for our planet.

7
00:00:36.812 --> 00:00:42.678
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

8
00:00:42.758 --> 00:00:48.583
By the end of this unit, you will be able
to name and describe the beach, the coast,

9
00:00:48.663 --> 00:00:52.097
the forest and the mountain using unit vocabulary.

10
00:00:52.177 --> 00:00:59.689
You will also explain the difference between weather,
climate and temperature, and describe today's weather.

11
00:00:59.769 --> 00:01:06.297
You will also form present perfect sentences
with have or has and the correct past participle.

12
00:01:06.377 --> 00:01:08.898
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

13
00:01:08.978 --> 00:01:15.932
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: climate,
weather, temperature, sunshine, froze, mountain.

14
00:01:16.012 --> 00:01:21.806
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

15
00:01:21.886 --> 00:01:28.139
The reading sequence includes Our Wonderful
Nature and A Poem: “Nature Is Our Home”.

16
00:01:28.219 --> 00:01:33.417
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

17
00:01:33.497 --> 00:01:37.941
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

18
00:01:38.021 --> 00:01:41.742
The first language focus is The Present Perfect Tense.

19
00:01:41.822 --> 00:01:47.795
We use the present perfect for something
that happened before but still matters today.

20
00:01:47.875 --> 00:01:54.341
When you say “I have explored a forest”, you
tell people what your life has already included.

21
00:01:54.421 --> 00:01:58.916
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

22
00:01:58.996 --> 00:02:04.310
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1 — Describe a Place in Nature.

23
00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:08.109
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

24
00:02:08.189 --> 00:02:15.858
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

25
00:02:15.938 --> 00:02:17.638
You are ready to begin.

26
00:02:17.718 --> 00:02:25.142
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

27
00:02:25.222 --> 00:02:32.800
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
